tion tests, because the plan names no rule to protect and no changed adapter. I didn't touch any production code, build file or existing test. I ran `dotnet format` on the two test files.\n\n**Decision for you:** the test's display name follows the story title. The shared-scenario check (which only runs when the specification checkout is supplied) will fail until that exact title is added to `../dca-sample-specification/scenarios.md` and to the Java suite. I didn't read the specification because it's outside this stage's inputs, and adding the scenario is sync work outside this story.","ttft_ms":2842,"type":"result","duration_ms":98325,"uuid":"6b88bf56-2418-4e54-a9de-2caa3d186afa","ttft_stream_ms":2452,"time_to_request_ms":39,"first_content_frame_ms":2452,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
